diff --git a/os/system/builder/llm/Properties.llm b/os/system/builder/llm/Properties.llm
index 41e7594ee..756fe9cdd 100644
--- a/os/system/builder/llm/Properties.llm
+++ b/os/system/builder/llm/Properties.llm
@@ -36,6 +36,11 @@ A value is written as the step writes it:
   "=="          a choice: one of the options listed for it, quoted
   goal.call(Name="X")   an action, where a property holds one
 
+A property whose type is open (shown as `: item`) may carry the value's own type, written before the `=`:
+`Name:type=value`. Use it when the step says WHAT the value is, not just its letters — `hash the file 'x.bin'`
+→ `crypto.hash(Data:path="x.bin")` (a path: the file's contents are hashed), where a plain `Data="x.bin"`
+would hash the text "x.bin". Only an open (`item`) slot takes a typed row, and only the type the step names.
+
 In `call X name=value`, `name` is what the called goal reads the value as (`%name%`), even when it is a plang word such as `module`, `file` or `goal`; it is never a module or action of the step.
 
 The arguments a step passes to a goal are one dict in Parameter:
@@ -59,6 +64,7 @@ Common steps, and their formal:
   call SendMail to=%email%, subject="Hi"          goal.call(Name="SendMail", Parameter={to: %email%, subject: "Hi"})
   foreach %orders%, call Ship order=%item%        loop.foreach(Collection=%orders%); goal.call(Name="Ship", Parameter={order: %item%})
   save %report% to file 'report.txt'              file.save(Path="report.txt", Value=%report%)
+  hash the file 'notes.txt' with sha256           crypto.hash(Data:path="notes.txt", Algorithm="sha256")
   if %age% >= 18, call Adult                      condition.if(Left=%age%, Operator=">=", Right=18) { goal.call(Name="Adult") }
   get https://example.com/rates, write to %rates% http.request(Url="https://example.com/rates"); variable.set(Name=%rates%, Value=%!data%)
   render "page.html", title=%title%, write to %html%
